{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3264","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3264","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3264\",\"parent_revision\":\"11f2d5c1ba2b8b6f4ecc346366658fe60730e0c1228f07c6e6a3a132bdeb4150\",\"root_revision\":\"11f2d5c1ba2b8b6f4ecc346366658fe60730e0c1228f07c6e6a3a132bdeb4150\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Docs\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-28\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n## Story\\n\\nAs a maintainer of the `backlog` skill, I want its runtime reference files to hold only content an executing agent needs, so that dead documentation about a removed system doesn't load into every consultation of that reference.\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/skills/backlog/references/known-patterns.md` contains an entire section, \\\"Legacy `.md` Format,\\\" explicitly labeled \\\"(Historical Reference Only)\\\" and stating outright that \\\"the implementation no longer exists.\\\" It documents bugs and fixes (with session dates, e.g. \\\"Session 2026-02-28\\\") in a system that has since been replaced (the file's own heading for the current section reads \\\"YAML Format (Current \u2014 Post Pe1f2a3b4 Migration)\\\").\\n\\nThe section also has two `SOURCE:` citations pointing to an internal migration identifier and a grep-based verification note, and a heading citing that same migration ID.\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\nThis is runtime reference content \u2014 loaded by an executing agent consulting this file for current backlog-item formatting patterns \u2014 not a maintainer-only document. A dead, ~50-line section about a system that \\\"no longer exists\\\" adds no actionable value to that agent and inflates the file for no operational benefit.\\n\\n## Observations\\n\\n- Flagged rather than fixed during a broader no-op/maintenance-note tightening pass, because this needs a real disposition decision (delete outright vs. relocate the 